# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
# Host credentials exported onto this repository's dispatches — the whole family, not
# `/.env` alone: a copy made before editing (`.env.bak`, `.env.2`) holds the same live
# token, and nothing downstream of a commit redacts a file sitting in the tree. The
# example file is documentation and is named back in, the way `/scratch/*` is below.
/.env*
!/.env.example
# Local Markdown plan authoring; onetaskgraph copies finished plans to the remote store.
/.plans/
# Unverified follow-up drafts (the `drafts` plan source); a follow-up agent verifies them
# after a run, and nothing here is repository content.
/.follow-ups/
# uv
# (uv.lock IS committed)

# Test / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

node_modules/
.nx/
dist/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Orchestrator run artifacts (reports written with -o land wherever the caller
# points; keep any local scratch out of the tree)
#
# `/scratch/*` and not `/scratch/`, because git will not re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded: the directory has to stay walkable for the one
# exception below to be reachable. Everything else directly in it is still ignored,
# and an ignored subdirectory's contents stay unreachable for re-inclusion — which is
# what keeps this an exception for one file rather than a hole for the whole tree.
/scratch/*
# The evidence behind a decision this branch delivers — that oneagentgraph 0.3.0 is
# not adopted — so it is tracked. Tracked was not enough: under `/scratch/` it sat
# outside both the llmlint diff tier, which honors this file, and the `wholeWorkspace`
# Nx key, so nothing judged it and editing it invalidated nothing. Naming it here is
# what puts it inside both.
!/scratch/issue-24-followups.md
/runs/

# The planner channel's envelope pass cache (config/onemessagebus.yaml): the bus's own
# record of envelopes the criteria bar passed, keyed on the bar, and never content.
/.cache/envelope-passes/

# Screenshot galleries (`just dag-ui-screens`). One directory per invocation, so two
# concurrent runs never write into each other's; they are evidence to look at, not
# repository content, and nothing here is ever compared against a checked-in image.
/.screenshots/

# Preserved command output (scripts/preserved-log.sh). Deliberately per-worktree
# and deliberately ignored: it is diagnostic evidence, not repository content.
/.logs/

# The fold checkpoint the engine resumes a run's state from instead of replaying its
# journal, and the run summary it caches beside it (`summary.json`: a reader folds a run
# once and caches what it folded). Both are derived, both are written by a **reader** —
# `just status`, `just host`, `just runs`, `onepipeline watch` — and the recorded runs
# under `tests/fixtures/timeline-runs/` are what this suite drives those readers over, so
# without this every such read leaves the working tree dirty and moves the
# `recipeWorkspace` key those fixtures are part of. Deleting one costs the next read its
# fold and nothing else.
/tests/fixtures/**/checkpoint.json
/tests/fixtures/**/summary.json
